WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
Day one is a check, not a lesson.

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:04.996
It shows you which guessing habit your child has.

3
00:00:05.696 --> 00:00:09.809
You hold the grown-up page. Your child gets the page with the big words.

4
00:00:10.259 --> 00:00:11.437
There are three parts.

5
00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:16.953
Part A. Your child reads eight words with no picture. Mark each word read right.

6
00:00:17.403 --> 00:00:23.283
Listen for one thing. If your child says a different word that starts with the same letter, circle that word.

7
00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:30.110
Part B. Each word has a picture above it, and the picture does not match. Do not tell your child yet.

8
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.694
If your child says the name of the picture, circle the word.

9
00:00:34.144 --> 00:00:38.556
Afterwards, tell your child the pictures were a trick. The letters tell you the word.

10
00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:44.820
Part C. Read the two sentences out loud once, and point to each word. Your child says them back.

11
00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.312
Then your child reads the same words alone, mixed up.

12
00:00:48.762 --> 00:00:54.341
A child who remembers lines can say the sentence, but cannot read its words in a new order.

13
00:00:54.791 --> 00:00:58.463
Do not teach, and do not correct today. Just listen and mark.

14
00:00:58.913 --> 00:01:04.630
Then read the yellow box at the bottom of your page, from the top. Stop at the first line that fits.

15
00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.672
That line names the habit, and tells you which days to do twice.

16
00:01:09.122 --> 00:01:17.787
One line is for the child who is not guessing at all, but cannot yet join sounds into a word. That child needs the blending plan first.

17
00:01:18.237 --> 00:01:22.915
Write the three numbers on the page, and keep it. You will look at it again on the last day.
